// GuardTalkContactsIconOverlay — F-ICON-CONTACTS
// Static RRO overriding com.android.contacts launcher icon (adaptive + legacy).
//
// TARGET: com.android.contacts (packages/apps/Contacts/AndroidManifest.xml
//   android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"  android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round").
//
// PARTITION MATCH: Contacts is `product_specific` + `privileged: true`
//   (packages/apps/Contacts/Android.bp; ships at product/priv-app/Contacts/).
//   On Android 14+ OverlayManager silently drops static RROs whose target
//   lives in a different partition than the overlay. This overlay MUST be
//   `product_specific: true` so it ships in /product/overlay/ alongside its
//   target.
//
// CERTIFICATE MATCH: Contacts is signed with the SHARED key
//   (`certificate: "shared"` in packages/apps/Contacts/Android.bp, verified
//   2026-06-30). The F-ICON-CONTACTS task brief stated "platform (Contacts is
//   platform-signed)" — that is INCORRECT per Law 7 (Structured Self-Doubt) /
//   Law 8 (Determinism); the canonical source (Android.bp) shows
//   `certificate: "shared"`. OverlayManager enables a static RRO that
//   overrides NON-overlayable resources (the legacy raster mipmaps + adaptive
//   foreground/background drawables are NOT declared <overlayable> in Contacts
//   — no overlayable.xml exists under packages/apps/Contacts/res/) only when
//   the overlay shares the target's signing certificate. This overlay uses
//   `certificate: "shared"` to match Contacts so the override wins at boot.
runtime_resource_overlay {
    name: "GuardTalkContactsIconOverlay",
    sdk_version: "current",
    product_specific: true,
    certificate: "shared",
}
